{
  "strategy": "The video appears to show a single static geometry diagram with on-screen instructional text. Retrieve the diagram frame directly, then use OCR to capture any labels/text and chart-style structural analysis to interpret the rectangle arrangement and the shaded region needed to compute the area.",
  "tool_calls": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "tool": "frame_retriever",
      "arguments": {
        "video_path": "VIDEO",
        "query": "static geometry diagram showing two white-outlined rectangles arranged in an L-shape on a black background, with a shaded region and math problem text",
        "timestamps": null,
        "num_frames": 3
      },
      "purpose": "Get the key frame(s) containing the full problem diagram in a stable state before reading text or interpreting the geometry.",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "tool": "ocr",
      "arguments": {
        "frame_path": "<STEP_1:frames>",
        "timestamp": null
      },
      "purpose": "Read any on-screen problem text, labels, dimensions, or answer choices visible in the retrieved diagram frames.",
      "depends_on": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "tool": "chart_analyzer",
      "arguments": {
        "frame_path": "<STEP_1:frames>",
        "timestamp": null,
        "query": "geometry diagram with two rectangles and a shaded region; identify the component shapes, how the shaded region relates to the rectangles, and any visible dimensions or equalities needed to compute the shaded area"
      },
      "purpose": "Interpret the structured diagram: determine the rectangle configuration, what region is shaded, and what geometric relationships are needed for the area calculation.",
      "depends_on": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "refinement_instructions": "Build the first trace from scratch using the retrieved diagram evidence. Use OCR as authoritative for any visible text, labels, dimensions, and answer options. Use chart_analyzer as authoritative for the diagram structure: which rectangles are present, how they share edges, and exactly which subregion is shaded. In the rewritten trace, first describe the full visible setup, then state the area facts implied by 'each rectangle is 10 square units,' then compute the shaded area only from diagram-grounded relationships. Do not infer an option by plausibility alone. If OCR or chart_analyzer reveals dimensions or partitions, cite those explicitly. If multiple retrieved frames differ, use the frame-level results and pick the frame that shows the most complete diagram state; do not merge inconsistent details across frames. Update the final answer to the option whose area matches the verified computation."
}
